post_id":"1370","description":"Just goofing off taking a slot line thru the rocks.","caption":"Roadside Elk","poi_name":"Below the portage/sieve","subject":"Shayne Day","author":"Brad Roberts","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6533","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6533"}},{"id":"6534","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1370","description":"Another cool slide on the elk.","caption":"Roadside Elk","poi_name":"","subject":"Shayne Day","author":"Brad Roberts","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6534","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6534"}},{"id":"6535","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"1370","description":"Fun slide with a left and right line.  Second run we went with the right line.","caption":"Roadside Elk","poi_name":"First big slide/falls","subject":"Brad Roberts","author":"Shayne Day","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/6535","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/6535"}},{"id":"3871","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4283","description":"","caption":"Lenny on the Elk","poi_name":"","subject":"Lenny Sheps","author":"Mark Mastalski","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3871","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3871"}},{"id":"3872","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4283","description":"","caption":"Logslide","poi_name":"","subject":"Mark Mastalski","author":"Mark Jankowski","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3872","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3872"}},{"id":"888627","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"891306","description":"This rapid looked like it might be a problem from above, but was rather smooth and enjoyable.","caption":"Cleaner than it looks","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/888627","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/888627"}},{"id":"888637","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"891317","description":"A typical rapid on the Elk River, roadside section. ","caption":"Elk Rapid","poi_name":null,"subject":null,"author":"","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/888637","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/888637"}},{"id":"3873","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4283","description":"Stay away from the far river left side of this drop.  It contains a nasty pin spot leading into one of the worst undercut walls you'll ever see.","caption":"Avoid far river left!","poi_name":"","subject":"Pin spot","author":"Mark Mastalski","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3873","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3873"}},{"id":"3874","ext":"jpeg","post_id":"4283","description":"The river will make a bend to the right when you see a cabin on the right side and a foot bridge.  Get out on river left and scout as shown here.","caption":"Get out and scout","poi_name":"","subject":"","author":"Mark Mastalski","poi_id":null,"photo_date":null,"updated_at":null,"url":{"medium":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/medium/3874","large":"https://api.americanwhitewater.org/image/images/big/3874"}}],"detail":{"id":"1067","permitUrl":null,"permitInfo":null,"description":"Carolina Whitewater, B.Benner\n\nThis is a fun one. Lots of good boat scoutable boogie water. Some good slides. A couple of large vertical drops. At one point in the first two miles the river completely disappears under a bunch of large boulders. The easy portage is river left (river right is someone's backyard). There are some undercuts and sieves to be avoided. This is a run that short creek boats were designed for!\n\nThere is an option of doing a short run from SR 1326 to the NC Hwy 194 Bridge. This gives you the top three miles of roadside water and a very easy shuttle.\n\n_Bradley - 2001_\n\nDon't miss the take-out. Just downstream lies Big Falls. Inadvertently running it could be way ugly.\n\n**Directions**\n\nFrom Elk Park:\n\nTake-Out: In downtown Elk Park look for the signs to Big Falls and follow them. Take Little Elk Creek Road (SR 1305) to the river. First bridge over water you come to is the take-out.\n\nPut-in: From Elk Park take Hwy 19 south to NC 194. Eventually you will cross the Elk. From there continue on to SR 1326. It will be a small turnoff on the right. Its easy to miss.","averageGradient":"130","maxGradient":"210","length":"3.5","correlations":[{"reachID":"1067","isPrimary":true,"correlationDetails":{"metric":"cfs","belowRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableRangeComment":null,"mediumRunnableRangeComment":null,"highRunnableRangeComment":null,"aboveRecommendedRangeComment":null,"lowRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"highRunnableAdjustedDifficulty":null,"beginLowRunnable":"400","beginMediumRunnable":null,"beginHighRunnable":null,"endHighRunnable":"1000"},"gaugeInfo":{"name":"WATAUGA RIVER NEAR SUGAR GROVE, NC","gaugeSource":"USGS","gaugeSourceIdentifier":"03479000","gaugeFetchStatus":"ACTIVE","latestFlowReading":{"value":"53","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"latestStageReading":{"value":"1.51","dateTime":"2026-05-12T02:15:00.000Z","qualifier":"NORMAL"},"location":{"latitude":"36.23916667","longitude":"-81.8222222"},"externalSourceLinks":{"sourceLink":{"url":"https://water.noaa.gov/gauges/03479000","text":"NOAA"},"secondaryLink":{"url":"https://waterdata.usgs.gov/monitoring-location/03479000/#parameterCode=00060&period=P7D","text":"US Geo